Named concept declarations (template<class T> concept X = ...).
CBMC skips concept constraints (treats as always satisfied).

Was KNOWNBUG since round 152 ("function must have return type"): a
requires-clause followed directly by the declaration's type name
(`requires SignedIntegral<T> T negate(T x)`) -- fixed 2026-09-23 in the
restricted constraint parser, see cpp20_requires_unparenthesized.
